{{Quote|I know Toydarians. Nothing goes on under their watch without them knowing.|Anakin Skywalker|<ref name="dou">{{TCW|A Death on Utapau}}</ref>}}
'''Toydarians''' were a [[Sentience|sentient]], winged [[species]] from the [[planet]] [[Toydaria]] in [[Hutt Space]]. In addition to their ability to fly, Toydarians were physically defined by their long snouts and webbed feet, and could resist [[Mind trick|mental manipulation]] from [[the Force]]. During the [[Clone Wars]], the Toydarians were ruled by [[King]] [[Katuunko]]. The Toydarians were, for a time, neutral during the Clone Wars, before eventually siding with the [[Galactic Republic]].

==Biology==
{{Quote|I'm a Toydarian! Mind tricks don't work on me, only money.|Watto, to Qui-Gon Jinn|<ref name="Episode I" />}}
A [[humanoid]] [[species]], Toydarians were fly-like, possessing wings, a [[Nose|snout]], and webbed feet.<ref name="Databank" /> Their wings allowed them to hover above the mud flats of their [[homeworld]].<ref name="VE" /> Like many other beings in [[the galaxy]], Toydarians started out life as infants but grew larger as they became older.<ref name="HRA 9">[[The High Republic Adventures (2021) 9|''The High Republic Adventures'' (2021) 9]]</ref> They had [[Color|blue]]<ref name="Episode I" /> and green skin tones<ref name="Ambush" /> with facial tusks beneath their trunk-like snouts. Toydarians were known to be strong-willed and resistant to [[Mind trick|mental manipulation]] with [[the Force]].<ref name="Databank" /><ref name="Episode I" /> The surviving [[Jedi Knight]] [[Grandea]], however, was able to exhibit such a skill in the mind trick that she could successfully manipulate a Toydarian with the [[Force power]].<ref name="Legacy of Vader 7">[[Legacy of Vader 7|''Legacy of Vader'' 7]]</ref>

==Society and culture==
{{Quote|Such despicable beings, the Toydarians.|Roman Herbane|<ref name="caros">''[[Catalyst: A Rogue One Novel]]''</ref>}}
Able to hover over the mud flats of [[Toydaria]],<ref name="VE" /> Toydarians made nests in the muck lake [[atmosphere]] of their homeworld,<ref name="Complete Locations">[[Star Wars: Complete Locations (2016)|''Star Wars: Complete Locations'']]</ref> but built their palaces on [[mountain]] peaks.<ref name="VE" /> Toydarians gathered in clans, and [[Toydarian clan bell]]s signified members of noble families.<ref name="Complete Locations" /> The species moved in flocks.<ref name="Bloodline">[[Bloodline (novel)|''Bloodline'']]</ref> During the era of the [[Clone Wars]], the Toydarians were governed by a [[monarchy]].<ref name="Supply Lines" />

==History==
Hailing from their homeworld of Toydaria,<ref name="Databank" /> the Toydarians were led by a monarchy during the last [[Standard decade|decades]] of the [[Galactic Republic]], and were ruled by [[King]] [[Katuunko]] as of the Clone Wars.<ref name="Ambush" />

[[File:KatuunkoPresiding-SL.png|thumb|left|260px|King Katuunko]]
In [[22 BBY]],<ref name="Date">''[[Star Wars: Galactic Atlas]]'' places the early events of the [[Battle of Ryloth]] and the [[mission to Rodia]] to [[22 BBY]]. As the episode this event takes place within takes place between the events of the pieces of media the other events are attached to according to {{SW|url=news/star-wars-the-clone-wars-chronological-episodeorder|text=''Star Wars: The Clone Wars'' Chronological Episode Order}}, this event must also take place in 22 BBY.</ref> during the Clone Wars between the [[Galactic Republic]] and [[Confederacy of Independent Systems]], the Republic, intent on negotiating terms with the Toydarian government, led a mission to the [[moon]] of [[Rugosa]] under the supervision of [[Jedi]] [[Grand Master]] [[Yoda]]. However, upon arriving in the [[Rugosa system|system]], Yoda's [[Consular-class cruiser (Charger c70 retrofit)|cruiser]] was [[Battle of Rugosa|ambushed]] by two Separatist [[Munificent-class star frigate|''Munificent''-class star frigates]] in an attempt made by the [[Dark Acolyte]], [[Asajj Ventress]], to force Yoda to flee the system and allow the Separatists to negotiate instead.<ref name="Ambush" />

Despite her attempts, Yoda and three [[clone trooper]]s managed to reach the surface, where they were forced to fight against Ventress's army of battle droids. After prolonged fighting between Yoda, the [[Cloning|clones]], and Ventress's [[droid]]s, the [[Jedi Master]] reached the [[Sith assassin]] and the Toydarian king, whose execution was ordered by Separatist [[Head of State|leader]], [[Count]] [[Dooku]], but was prevented by Yoda, which forced Ventress to flee Rugosa and allow the Republic to successfully negotiate Toydaria's alignment in the war.<ref name="Ambush" />

Later in the war, Katuunko was [[Death|killed]] by the [[Sith apprentice]] [[Savage Opress]].<ref name="Witches">{{TCW|Witches of the Mist}}</ref>

==Toydarians in the galaxy==
The Toydarian [[Watto]] operated as a [[junk dealer]] on [[Tatooine]] during the lead-up to the war, and owned [[Slavery|slaves]] including [[Shmi Skywalker Lars|Shmi Skywalker]] and her son [[Anakin Skywalker|Anakin]].<ref name="Episode I" />

During the [[Imperial Era]], [[Walisi]] was a Toydarian [[merchant]] who ran [[Walisi's Elegant and Exotic Artifacts]] with his [[protocol droid]] [[RT-3PO]]. However, Walisi went on to be [[Walisi's kidnapping|kidnapped]] by [[Wrecker (mercenary)|Wrecker]], who himself was a Toydarian. Unlike Walisi, Wrecker was a [[mercenary]] leader, having been hired by the surviving [[Nightsisters|Nightsister]] [[Jerserra]] to kidnap Walisi and steal the ''[[Tragic Hope]]'', an artifact that contained the [[Nardithi Nightsisters]]' [[Nardithi Cluster]], before the merchant could sell it.<ref name="GoD">''[[Ghosts of Dathomir]]''</ref>

[[Zabaka]], a female Toydarian, owned a [[Toydarian Toymaker|toyshop]] in [[Black Spire Outpost]], [[Batuu]].<ref name="Galaxy's Edge: Black Spire">''[[Galaxy's Edge: Black Spire]]''</ref>

